      "voiceover": {
        "text": "Link every structure to what it makes possible. Bones are levers and joints are fulcrums, so a muscle's pull becomes movement. Joint class decides how much movement exists. The shape of the bone ends decides which actions. Cartilage, fluid and ligaments keep it smooth and safe. And bone remodels with load. The classic mistake is a labelled list of bones with nothing about movement."
